{
    "architecture": "aarch64",
    "context": "Cached native procfs task-path invalidation, without directory-list polling. Root/UID1000 in initial/one-level PID namespaces each run [270,180,180,99,27,90] controls across three mounts, self/numeric parents, stat/status/directory leaves and five libc/raw pathname/openat forms, including native upper words and original/dup/CLOEXEC parent handles. Total3384 controls per architecture; baselines fail792. Two live worker threads are observed by tgkill signal0; joined retirement waits for independently observed ESRCH without procfs probes. Main/surviving siblings stay visible, unrelated child IDs are absent from parent task membership, WNOWAIT zombie main paths stay present until reap, then cached paths return ENOENT. Retained parent/stat/directory descriptors preserve dev/ino/mode and descriptor flags after pruning. The PID-table helper returns only a scalar membership verdict under pid_lock; it borrows no pointer, allocates nothing and releases that lock before existing namespace pruning/unref. Lookup validates the cached child selectively rather than pruning from a transient try-locked thread-list snapshot. Existing detached nodes/resources remain retained, even at refcount0; no reclamation path is added. Four200-cycle warm/settled cohorts measure repeated live/missing task paths and temporary aliases with all slabs/largepages flat, not task/mount churn. Four completed production builds, five candidate cases, eight host files, 63 frozen kernel inputs, exact four-function generated-C scope, same native ELF Linux6.12.51 references and independent lifetime review are bound. Assertion and passing-as-baseline negative controls execute. Exact f635 compiler rebuilt in a private worktree after its baked shared source directory disappeared; local compiler/GC/TCC and tracked source pins are frozen. Earlier kernels/C/build logs are preserved as diagnostics. Original baseline/candidate probe source/C/ELFs and separate preflight C/ELF match exactly; whole-C comparison logs are empty without normalization. Existing allocation allowance refusals remain. PID/TID reuse, exact concurrent detach after a positive check, leader-only exit, general process-root cache invalidation, deep namespaces, tree reclamation/churn, GNU/translated/ELF32 and three broad roadmap gates remain separate.",
